Then known as the Dutch Republic, its wealth and power flourished through the importing of goods from overseas, with huge ships sent to Asia and Africa to bring back textiles, teas, grains and spices. A popular proverb among the Dutch during this period was, Jesus Christ is good, but trade is better. The Dutch East India Company, known in its homeland as the VOC, was a chartered company established to coordinate trade in India and other countries throughout Southeast Asia. Monopolising all trade to the east, it boasted tens of thousands of employees and its own
当时被称为荷兰共和国，其财富和权力通过从海外进口货物而蓬勃发展，巨大的船只被派往亚洲和非洲带回纺织品、茶叶、谷物和香料。当时荷兰人中流行的一句俗语是：“耶稣基督很好，但贸易更好。”荷兰东印度公司在其国内被称为VOC，是一家旨在协调印度及东南亚其他国家贸易的特许公司。它垄断了所有通往东方的贸易，拥有数万名员工和自己的

