Word of Lucretia Yarn's assault reached the Batavia's commander, upper merchant Francisco who began investigating the matter. Upper merchants were VOC officials who were assigned overall responsibility for a particular fleet. Their task was to ensure the voyage would be profitable for the company's directors. Second in command was the ship's captain, followed by the upper merchant's deputy known as the under merchant. Francisco Pelsart was aged in his early 30s and was a long-time VOC employee, having
