00:15:45.000 --> 00:16:22.000
As it was unclear whether the tide was high or low, the crew wondered whether they might have simply run aground in shallows and would be able to float back out to sea once the water level rose. But after waiting several hours, it became clear that the collision had taken place at high tide. Falling water levels revealed they were surrounded by rocks, reefs and small islands. The impact had careened the ship half out of the ocean, with sharp coral tearing away its rudder and gouging its timber sides.
由于不清楚当时是涨潮还是落潮，船员们想知道他们可能只是在浅滩上搁浅，一旦水位上升就能漂回大海。但在等待了几个小时后，人们发现碰撞发生在涨潮时分，这一点变得很清楚。下降的水位显示他们周围环绕着岩石、礁石和小岛。撞击使船有一半冲出了海洋，锋利的珊瑚撕裂了船舵，并在其木制船体上凿出了大洞。

24
00:16:22.000 --> 00:17:06.000
Several frightened individuals jumped overboard and either drowned or were pierced by the sharp coral below. The crew began discarding cannons and gunners to lighten the Batavia's load, and just after dawn they cut its main mast down as well. Historians were later determined that the Batavia struck a shoal called Morning Reef in the northern most cluster of the Abrolis, a network of 122 barren, windswept islands and associated coral reefs in the Indian Ocean. They are located roughly 60km west of what is today the city of Geraldton in Western Australia.
几个惊恐的人跳进海里，要么淹死了，要么被底部的尖锐珊瑚刺穿。船员们开始丢弃大炮和炮手以减轻“巴达维亚”号的载重，黎明刚过，他们也砍倒了主桅杆。历史学家后来确定，“巴达维亚”号撞上了阿博洛霍斯群岛最北端的一处名为“早晨礁”的浅滩，这是一个由122个贫瘠、风吹日晒的岛屿以及印度洋相关珊瑚礁组成的群岛网络。它们位于现今西澳大利亚州杰拉尔顿市以西约60公里处。

25
00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:56.000
There are three distinct groups of islands, all of which have little in the way of vegetation or wildlife, aside from a few sea lions and birds. Seven hours after the collision, as preparations were underway to safely relocate Batavia's passengers, the ship burst open below the waterline and its hull began filling with water. The ship's crew began rowing the passengers away in the Batavia's longboat, an open vessel capable of holding 40 people and its yaw, a sailboat that could carry 23. They were set down on an island about 2km from the shipwreck. It was a tiny, hard and flat land mass with no vegetation, sand or shelter.
这里有三个截然不同的岛屿群，除了少量的海狮和鸟类外，所有岛屿几乎都没有植被或野生动物。碰撞发生七小时后，正当人们准备安全转移“巴达维亚”号的乘客时，船在水线下方爆裂，船体开始进水。船员们开始用“巴达维亚”号的长艇（一种可容纳40人的开放式船只）和 Yaw（一艘可载23人的帆船）将乘客划走。他们被安置在距离沉船约2公里处的一个岛屿上。这是一块极小、坚硬且平坦的陆地，没有植被、沙子或庇护所。

26
00:17:56.000 --> 00:18:46.000
Broken and sharp coral pieces lay all over the ground, making it difficult to walk on. By dusk, a number of people had been transferred to the island, including all of the women and children. 150 pints of drinking water, barrels of wine, meat and bread, and a casket full of valuable trade goods such as jewellery, gold and precious stones were also transported to land. Rescue work paused at night when it became too dark to see. Only 120 people still remained on the slowly crumbling Batavia. At dawn the following morning, efforts to retrieve those still stranded on the Batavia
破碎而锋利的珊瑚碎片铺满地面，使人寸步难行。到了黄昏，许多人已被转移到岛上，包括所有的妇女和儿童。150品脱的饮用水、一桶桶的葡萄酒、肉和面包，以及装满珠宝、黄金和宝石等珍贵贸易品的小箱子也被运送到陆地上。夜幕降临、能见度变差时，救援工作暂停。只有120人仍然留在缓缓解体的“巴达维亚”号上。第二天黎明，检索仍滞留在“巴达维亚”号上人员的工作

