recommenced. The small island closest to the ship became overcrowded, so 180 men, women and children were moved to a larger land mass, roughly 800 metres away, that had a sandy beach. They were given a limited supply of food, while Commander Pelsart, Captain Jacobs, all of the senior VOC company officials, a number of sailors, two women and one infant, remained on the smaller island with the longboat and yaw. Commander Pelsart was convinced to travel to the Australian mainland to find supplies. As the journey would require a couple of days' preparation, he opted to explore other nearby
重新开始。离船最近的小岛变得拥挤不堪，因此180名男人、女人和儿童被转移到大约800米外、拥有沙滩的较大陆地上。他们获得了有限的食物供应，而佩尔萨特指挥官、雅各布斯船长、所有东印度公司的高级官员、多名水手、两名妇女和一个婴儿，则与长艇和小帆船一起留在了较小的岛上。佩尔萨特指挥官被说服前往澳大利亚大陆寻找补给。由于这段旅程需要几天的准备时间，他选择在此期间探索附近的其他

