00:21:36.000 --> 00:22:11.000
Upon learning of Commander Pelsart's departure, the near-200 survivors on the Big Island were left devastated. They accused their leader of abandoning them and dubbed the small inlet where Pelsart had camped, Trader's Island. Their own island, which measured 270 metres wide and half a kilometre long, was named Batavia's Graveyard. Then Mike Dash described it as a strip of coral rubble, where the only living thing was the wind.
得知佩尔萨特指挥官离开后，大岛上近200名幸存者感到大受打击。他们指责领袖抛弃了他们，并将佩尔萨特曾扎营的小海湾称为“商人岛”。他们自己的岛屿长半公里、宽270米，被命名为“巴达维亚的墓地”。麦克·达什（Mike Dash）将其描述为“一条珊瑚碎石带，唯一的生物只有风”。

