00:22:11.000 --> 00:22:59.000
The shipwreck survivors landed there at the beginning of the Southern Hemisphere's winter, which regularly battered the area with storms and fierce gales. Of those stranded on Batavia's graveyard, at least 100 were VOC soldiers or sailors, while more than a dozen others were men with trade experience such as carpenters and blacksmiths. There were 21 women, the majority of whom were wives of the crew, a number of teenagers and children, and two infants who were born during the voyage. Most of the population's food and water supplies were depleted within a day, and anxieties only increased when Commander Pelsart sailed away with the other VOC officials.
海难幸存者在南半球冬季开始时登陆该地，该地区经常受到风暴和狂风的袭击。在滞留在“巴达维亚墓地”的人中，至少有100名东印度公司的士兵或水手，另外还有十多名具有木匠和铁匠等贸易经验的人。这里有21名妇女，其中大多数是船员的妻子，一些青少年和儿童，以及两个在航行期间出生的婴儿。该地大部分的人口食物和水供应在一天内就耗尽了，而当佩尔萨特指挥官与其他东印度公司官员扬帆远去时，焦虑感只增不减。

