00:45:04.000 --> 00:45:49.000
nails hammered into the ants, collected lumps of coral to throw it intruders, and made their own morning stars from wreckage that had washed up. Hayes had the advantage of being a skilled leader with strong soldiers and a sound understanding of battle tactics. The only way to access their island was from the neighbouring island's sandbank at Low Tide, ensuring the mutineers wouldn't be able to launch a surprise attack. Hayes constructed a two-room fort from limestone and coral slabs that overlooked the sandbank, allowing his men to keep a watch for invaders and take shelter from any potential threat.
锤入蚂蚁的钉子，收集珊瑚块扔给入侵者，并用冲刷上岸的残骸制作了自己的晨星锤。海耶斯拥有作为一名熟练领袖的优势，拥有强大的士兵和对战斗战术的健全理解。进入他们岛屿的唯一途径是在退潮时从邻近岛屿的沙洲进入，这确保了叛变者无法发起偷袭。海耶斯用石灰石和珊瑚板建造了一个两室堡垒，俯瞰着沙洲，使他的手下能够监视入侵者并躲避任何潜在的威胁。

65
00:45:49.000 --> 00:46:29.000
Two days after the July 21 massacre, Cornelius made a move against those on the Highland. In a seemingly friendly letter addressed to Private Hayes' small militia, Cornelius referred to those who had fled to the Highland as evil doers who were banished from Batavia's graveyard. He claimed they had left without permission and ordered they be returned to him, along with the boat that Ari's yants had stolen. Hayes didn't believe Cornelius' claims and instead imprisoned the mutineer who delivered the letter.
7月21日大屠杀两天后，科尼利乌斯对高地的人采取了行动。在一封写给海耶斯列兵小型民兵的看似友好的信中，科尼利乌斯将逃往高地的人称为被驱逐出巴达维亚墓地的作恶者。他声称他们在没有许可的情况下离开，并命令将他们以及阿里·扬斯偷走的船一起归还给他。海耶斯不相信科尼利乌斯的说法，而是关押了送信的叛变者。

66
00:46:29.000 --> 00:47:01.000
After several days passed with no reply or sign of his messenger, Cornelius launched an attack. He sent his two chief executioners, David Zavunk and Cornrat Van Hyssen, to the island, with 20 other mutineers. Yet, they were forced to retreat as their adversaries had observed them approach and took up arms. On August 5, Zavunk and Van Hyssen attempted another incursion, this time with all the mutineers.
在没有收到回信或信使迹象的几天后，科尼利乌斯发起了攻击。他派他的两名首席刽子手大卫·扎温克和康拉特·范·海森以及其他20名叛变者前往该岛。然而，他们被迫撤退，因为他们的对手已经观察到他们接近并拿起武器。8月5日，扎温克和范·海森再次试图入侵，这次带上了所有的叛变者。

67
00:47:01.000 --> 00:47:44.000
As they waded through the shallows towards the island, they were once again met by the well-prepared soldiers and were forced to turn back. Meanwhile, the inhabitants of Batavia's graveyard continued to suffer. By August, only seven women remained alive and all were forced into sexual slavery. Cornelius became fixated on Lucretia yarns, who had already endured a demeaning assault at the hands of the mutineers while on the Batavia. He attempted to seduce her by writing her poems and giving her wine, but she rejected his advances.
当他们蹚过浅滩向小岛进发时，他们再次遇到了准备充分的士兵，并被迫折返。与此同时，巴达维亚墓地的居民继续遭受苦难。到了8月，只剩下七名女性活着，全部被迫沦为性奴隶。科尼利乌斯迷上了卢克雷蒂亚·扬斯（Lucretia Yarns），她在巴达维亚号上时就已经忍受了叛变者侮辱性的袭击。他通过给她写诗和送酒来试图勾引她，但她拒绝了他的追求。

68
00:47:44.000 --> 00:48:27.000
After two weeks, Cornelius lost his temper and complained to David Zavunk about the matter. Zavunk then threatened Lucretia with death if she didn't comply with Cornelius' wishes, so she submitted to his will. That same month, a boy was blindfolded under the guise of a joke, only to be decapitated. Hans Hardens, who had already endured the murder of his six-year-old daughter, Hylatrine, also lost his wife when she was strangled with her own hair ribbon. The man who led the survivor's prior to Cornelius' arrival was stabbed with a pike
两周后，科尼利乌斯发脾气，并向大卫·扎温克抱怨此事。扎温克随后威胁卢克雷蒂亚，如果不顺从科尼利乌斯的意愿就杀死她，于是她屈服于他的意志。同月，一个男孩在玩笑的幌子下被蒙上双眼，随后被斩首。汉斯·哈登斯（Hans Hardens）已经忍受了他六岁女儿海拉特林（Hylatrine）被谋杀的痛苦，他的妻子也因被自己的头发丝带勒死而丧生。在科尼利乌斯到来之前领导幸存者的那个人被长矛刺死……

69
00:48:27.000 --> 00:49:09.000
and sword, then hidden ahead with a morning star. The mutineers openly discussed whom they would like to murder next, and people were not permitted to mourn for their loved ones. Following the massacre of Geisbert Bastien's family, mutineers discovered him crying and stated, Be silent, or you go the same way. Geisbert's life was regularly threatened, but Cornelius believed he might prove a useful bargaining chip in the battle against the Highland, so he was kept alive.
和剑，然后用晨星锤藏在前面。叛变者公开讨论他们接下来想谋杀谁，人们不准为他们的亲人哀悼。在盖斯伯特·巴斯蒂安兹一家被屠杀后，叛变者发现他在哭泣并说：“闭嘴，否则你也会落得同样的下场。”盖斯伯特的生命经常受到威胁，但科尼利乌斯相信他在与高地的战斗中可能会被证明是一个有用的谈判筹码，所以他被留了下来。

70
00:49:09.000 --> 00:49:48.000
By late August, winter was drawing to an end, and it was raining less, resulting in depleting water supplies. Cornelius attempted yet another charge on the Highland, this time with a more deceptive approach. On September 1, he sent Geisbert Bastien's to negotiate a peace treaty with Private Hayes, who agreed to receive the mutineers the following day. On September 2, the entire population of Batavia's graveyard, now reduced to 32 men and six women, travelled to the Highland with Cornelius.
到了8月下旬，冬天即将结束，雨水减少，导致水资源供应耗尽。科尼利乌斯对高地进行了又一次进攻，这次采用了更具欺骗性的方法。9月1日，他派遣盖斯伯特·巴斯蒂安兹去与海耶斯列兵协商和平条约，后者同意第二天接待叛变者。9月2日，巴达维亚墓地的全体人口（此时已减少到32名男子和6名妇女）与科尼利乌斯一起前往高地。

71
00:49:48.000 --> 00:50:32.000
They watched from the sandbank between islands as Cornelius and five of his most loyal followers continued onwards. They gifted their adversaries new clothes and red wine, which were well received. As Cornelius and Hayes engaged in peace talks, the mutineers offered the soldiers from the Highland jewels and money to switch sides. In response, the soldiers launched a surprise attack, arresting Cornelius and four of his men, including David Zavunk and Cornrat Van Heisen. One mutineer named Vowter Loos managed to escape and reach a small boat.
他们从岛屿之间的沙洲上看着科尼利乌斯和他的五个最忠实的追随者继续前进。他们向对手赠送了新衣服和红酒，受到了热烈的欢迎。当科尼利乌斯和海耶斯进行和平谈判时，叛变者向高地的士兵提供珠宝和金钱以转换阵营。作为回应，士兵们发起了突袭，逮捕了科尼利乌斯和他的四名手下，包括大卫·扎温克和康拉特·范·海森。一个名叫沃特·洛斯（Vowter Loos）的叛变者设法逃脱并到达了一艘小船。

72
00:50:32.000 --> 00:51:16.000
The mutineers waiting on the sandbank made a beeline for the soldiers, though they had to run almost half a kilometre to reach them. They vastly outnumbered the soldiers, so Private Webby Hayes ordered the immediate execution of Cornelius' captured followers to scare the rest of the mutineers away. Both David Zavunk and Cornrat Van Heisen were among those killed. The brutal display caused the approaching mutineers to retreat back to Batavia's graveyard, taking the innocent survivors with them. Veronimus Cornelius, now a prisoner of the Highland, was placed in a limestone pit that
在沙洲上等待的叛变者径直冲向士兵，尽管他们不得不跑将近半公里才能到达他们身边。他们的数量远远超过士兵，因此列兵韦比·海耶斯下令立即处决科尼利乌斯被俘的追随者，以吓退其余的叛变者。大卫·扎温克和康拉特·范·海森都在被杀之列。这种残酷的展示导致逼近的叛变者撤回巴达维亚墓地，带走了无辜的幸存者。现在成为高地囚犯的维罗尼穆斯·科尼利乌斯被关进了一个石灰石坑里……

73
00:51:16.000 --> 00:52:02.000
functioned as a cell. He spent his days plucking feathers from birds that the soldiers had hunted. Over on Batavia's graveyard, a new ruler was elected from the mutineer's ranks, 24-year-old Vowter Loos. Under his authority, the murders ceased and women were no longer abused. But Cornelius now gone, a number of men abandoned the cause, leaving fewer than 20 loyalists. Two weeks later, supplies on Batavia's graveyard were running low. In a desperate bid to gain access to their water and food, Loos declared war on the Highlands.
充当牢房。他整天拔着士兵们猎杀的鸟类的羽毛。在巴达维亚墓地，从叛变者的行列中选出了一位新统治者，24岁的沃特·洛斯。在他的权威下，谋杀停止了，妇女不再被虐待。但科尼利乌斯现在走了，许多人放弃了这个事业，只剩下不到20名忠诚者。两周后，巴达维亚墓地的物资快要用完了。为了绝望地获得水和食物，洛斯向高地宣战。

74
00:52:02.000 --> 00:52:52.000
The battle commenced at 9am on September 17. Though the remaining mutineers were now vastly outnumbered and didn't have the military experience of their opponents, they did have two muskets, each capable of firing one round per minute. Private Webby Hayes and his men took cover behind rocks and in their fort, but the mutineers still managed to wound four soldiers, one of whom later died from his injuries. The confrontation continued for several hours, until suddenly, in the early afternoon, a ship appeared on the horizon. Commander Francisco Pelsart and his group of 48 survivors had sailed for almost a month
战斗于9月17日上午9点开始。尽管剩下的叛变者现在人数远远落后，并且没有对手的军事经验，但他们确实有两支滑膛枪，每支每分钟可以发射一发子弹。列兵韦比·海耶斯和他的手下躲在岩石后和堡垒里，但叛变者仍然设法打伤了四名士兵，其中一人后来因伤势过重死亡。对峙持续了几个小时，直到突然间，在下午早些时候，一艘船出现在地平线上。指挥官弗朗西斯科·佩尔萨特（Francisco Pelsart）和他的48名幸存者小组航行了近一个月……

75
00:52:52.000 --> 00:53:33.000
in an effort to reach the Batavia settlement in Indonesia for help. They suffered no losses over the course of their journey and successfully reached the Dutch settlement on July 7, 1629. Two days later, Pelsart was summoned to appear before the VOC's council to account for the loss of the company's new flagship vessel and its precious cargo. Pelsart described the manner in which the Batavia had crashed into the reef, explaining that the majority of people on board had survived and they had managed to recover its most valuable items.
为了到达印度尼西亚的巴达维亚定居点寻求帮助。他们在整个航行过程中没有人员伤亡，并于1629年7月7日成功抵达荷兰定居点。两天后，佩尔萨特被传唤在VOC委员会面前作证，以解释公司新旗舰船只及其珍贵货物的损失。佩尔萨特描述了巴达维亚号撞上礁石的方式，解释说船上的大多数人都幸存下来，并且他们设法捞回了最宝贵的物品。

76
00:53:33.000 --> 00:54:09.000
Among those who accompanied Pelsart to Batavia was his longtime adversary, Captain Aryan Yacobes. He was held accountable for his actions aboard the Batavia, including orchestrating the attack on Lucretia Yarnes in a failed bid at mutiny. Both Haye and Batavia's Bosun, Yarn Avertz, who Lucretia identified as the ringleader, were arrested. After being tortured, Avertz confessed to his part in the mutiny and the assault of Lucretia and was executed by hanging.
陪同佩尔萨特前往巴达维亚的人中有他的老对手阿里安·雅各布斯船长（Captain Aryan Yacobes）。他对自己在巴达维亚号上的行为负责，包括在未遂的叛变中策划了对卢克雷蒂亚·扬斯的袭击。海耶和巴达维亚号的水手长扬·阿韦茨（Yarn Avertz）都被捕了，卢克雷蒂亚认出他是首领。经过酷刑折磨后，阿韦茨承认了他参与叛变和袭击卢克雷蒂亚，并被绞死。

77
00:54:09.000 --> 00:54:56.000
Captain Yacobes was ordered to stand trial for the faulty navigation that led to the Batavia becoming shipwrecked and his role in, quote, a gross evil and public assault. Captain Pelsart was granted another VOC ship named the Sardam to rescue the survivors he'd left behind and to recover as much cargo as possible. He departed Batavia on July 15 with a small crew and began sailing back towards the Abrolos Islands. By August 10, they were less than 80km from the shipwrecked site, but a navigation miscalculation as well as poor weather made it difficult to find the islands.
雅各布斯船长被命令因导致巴达维亚号失事的错误导航以及他在“重大罪行和公开袭击”中所扮演的角色而接受审判。佩尔萨特船长获准使用另一艘名为萨达姆号（Sardam）的VOC船只，去营救他留下的幸存者并尽可能多地捞回货物。他于7月15日带着一小队船员从巴达维亚出发，开始向阿布罗洛斯群岛（Abrolos Islands）返航。到8月10日，他们距离船难地点不到80公里，但导航计算错误以及糟糕的天气使得寻找这些岛屿变得困难。

78
00:54:56.000 --> 00:55:38.000
It took more than a month for them to orientate themselves. By September 13, the rescuers finally reached the northern end of the island chain. Three days later, on the evening of September 16, they sighted what remained of the Batavia and steered towards it the next morning. They dropped anchor at approximately midday on September 17, three kilometres from the highland and six and a half kilometres from Batavia's graveyard. As soon as the mutineers caught sight of the rescue ship, they ceased their attack on the highland.
他们花了 一个多月的时间才确定方向。到9月13日，救援人员终于到达了群岛的最北端。三天后的9月16日傍晚，他们看到了巴达维亚号的残骸，并在第二天早上朝它驶去。他们在9月17日大约中午时分抛锚，距离高地三公里，距离巴达维亚墓地六点五公里。叛变者一看到救援船，就停止了对高地的攻击。

79
00:55:38.000 --> 00:56:22.000
A boat was sighted rowing from the ship towards the smaller of the two highland islands, which sat south from where the battle was being waged. A number of the mutineers who were still dedicated to Cornelius's plan of commandeering a rescue vessel immediately set sail for the Sardin. At the same time, private Webby Hayes and three of his men raced to their own makeshift boat, hoping that they would be able to reach the rescuers first. The two groups began frantically rowing, trying to beat one another there. Commander Pelsart, along with several crew members, had loaded one of the Sardin's boats
人们看到一艘船从船上划向两个高地岛屿中较小的一个，该岛位于正在进行的战斗南面。一些仍然致力于科尼利乌斯征用救援船计划的叛变者立即起航前往萨丁号。与此同时，列兵韦比·海耶斯和他的三名手下冲向他们自己拼凑的船，希望他们能首先到达救援人员那里。两组人开始拼命划船，试图抢在对方前面到达。佩尔萨特指挥官和几名船员将萨丁号的一艘船装满了……

80
00:56:22.000 --> 00:57:07.000
with supplies such as bread and water and headed towards the nearest visible land. Just as they reached its shores and disembarked, a boat carrying four men drew close. One of the men leapt out and shouted at them. Welcome, but go back aboard immediately, for there is a party of miscreants on the islands near the wreck who have the intention to seize the yacht. The man was Private Webby Hayes. He quickly informed Pelsart of the events that had taken place over the past few months. Pelsart set back out for the Sardin to warn the remainder of his crew.
带着面包和水等补给品，朝最近可见的陆地驶去。就在他们到达海岸并下船时，一艘载着四个男人的船靠近了。其中一个人跳出来对他们喊道：“欢迎，但请立即返回船上，因为在残骸附近的岛屿上有一群恶棍，他们打算劫持游艇。”这个人就是列兵韦比·海耶斯。他迅速将过去几个月发生的事件告知了佩尔萨特。佩尔萨特再次出发前往萨丁号，以警告其余船员。

81
00:57:07.000 --> 00:57:51.000
As he neared the ship, he saw the mutineers were also rapidly approaching in their boat. When the mutineers boarded the Sardin, they were greeted by guns and pikes. Pelsart had made it aboard just in time to alert the crew of the ambush. The mutineers surrendered and were arrested. During interrogations, they revealed they had killed more than 100 men, women and children under the order of Euronymous Cornelius. Some also admitted to being part of the original mutiny on the Batavia, revealing that Captain Ariane Jacobs had been one of the masterminds behind it.
当他靠近船只时，他看到叛变者也乘船迅速逼近。当叛变者登上萨丁号时，迎接他们的是枪支和长矛。佩尔萨特及时登上了船，向船员们拉响了伏击警报。叛变者投降并被捕。在审讯期间，他们透露他们在尤尼穆斯·科尼利乌斯的命令下杀害了100多名男女老少。一些人还承认自己是巴达维亚号最初叛变的一部分，并透露阿里安·雅各布斯船长是幕后黑手之一。

82
00:57:51.000 --> 00:58:37.000
Cornelius was retrieved from his limestone prison and taken aboard the Sardin. Upon seeing the bound man, Commander Pelsart looked at his former deputy with great sorrow, as he was, quote, such a scoundrel, cause of so many disasters and of the shedding of human blood. Cornelius tried to absolve himself of any guilt by implicating his various followers in the mutiny and murders, but his claims were rejected and he was locked up in a cell. The following morning, Pelsart and several armed soldiers went to Batavia's graveyard to arrest the remaining mutineers and rescue the survivors.
科尼利乌斯从石灰石监狱中被带出，带上了萨达姆号。看到这个被绑着的男人，佩尔萨特指挥官怀着极大的悲痛看着他的前副手，因为他“真是个无赖，是那么多灾难和流血事件的根源”。科尼利乌斯试图通过将其各种追随者牵连到叛变和谋杀中来为自己开脱罪责，但他的说法遭到拒绝，他被关进了牢房。第二天早上，佩尔萨特和几个武装士兵前往巴达维亚墓地逮捕剩余的叛变者并营救幸存者。

83
00:58:37.000 --> 00:59:18.000
They discovered crucial pieces of evidence on the island, including several oaths that Cornelius had made his followers sign. Dutch law at the time dictated that justice needed to be meted out as quickly as possible, so it was decided that the trials of the mutiny's ringleaders would be carried out on the islands where the crimes had taken place. Pelsart and five other high-ranking officials from the Sardin and the Batavia formed a council and began proceedings. While the survivors were housed on the Sardin, the accused mutineers were kept prisoner on
他们在岛上发现了关键的证据，包括科尼利乌斯强迫他的追随者签署的几份誓言。当时的荷兰法律规定，正义需要尽快伸张，因此决定对叛变头目进行审判，地点就在犯罪发生的小岛上。佩尔萨特和来自萨达姆号和巴达维亚号的其他五名高级官员组成了一个委员会，并开始了诉讼程序。幸存者被安置在萨达姆号上，而被告叛变者则被关押在……

84
00:59:18.000 --> 01:00:00.000
Seales Island, far away from everybody else. The defendants had no lawyers, so the trial solely consisted of Pelsart questioning witnesses. Thus only a few of the perpetrators would admit to their crimes. Torture was used to elicit confessions from the others, including Cornelius. Interrogators would strap the individual to a frame, then slowly pour water over their head until it covered their faces and hindered their ability to breathe. They were then forced to drink the water, which led to extreme bloating and fainting if the torture lasted for an extended period.
西尔斯岛，远离所有人。被告没有律师，因此审判完全由佩尔萨特审问证人组成。因此只有少数肇事者会承认他们的罪行。酷刑被用来从其他人（包括科尼利乌斯）那里诱供。审讯人员会将个人绑在架子上，然后慢慢将水倒在他们的头上，直到水盖住他们的脸并妨碍他们的呼吸能力。然后他们被迫喝水，如果酷刑持续时间较长，这会导致极度腹胀和昏迷。

85
